{"id":"a79cd0c61a8bf7df","group":"17","path":"17/17-thm-los-vaught.md","title":"Łoś–Vaught Test","display":"thm-los-vaught — Łoś–Vaught Test","type":"theorem","metadata":{"numbering_status":"local atom identifier; not the book result number","source_verification":"pending exact book correspondence; local formulation reviewed, not source-verified","type":"theorem","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-thm-los-vaught","aliases":["17-thm-los-vaught"],"display":"thm-los-vaught — Łoś–Vaught Test","depends_on":["[[17-df-language-cardinality]]","[[17-df-sentence]]","[[17-df-model]]","[[17-df-theory-properties]]","[[17-df-categoricity]]","[[17-df-omega-stability]]","[[17-df-cardinal-arithmetic]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","legacy_label":"17-thm-7.1.2","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"numbering_status","html":"local atom identifier; not the book result number"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"pending exact book correspondence; local formulation reviewed, not source-verified"},{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-thm-los-vaught"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-thm-los-vaught</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-los-vaught — Łoś–Vaught Test"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e8f9375543fc2e7d\" href=\"?note=e8f9375543fc2e7d\" title=\"17-df-language-cardinality\">17-df-language-cardinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1280f7fa724c1502\" href=\"?note=1280f7fa724c1502\" title=\"17-df-sentence\">17-df-sentence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"bd7acd1192e46962\" href=\"?note=bd7acd1192e46962\" title=\"17-df-theory-properties\">17-df-theory-properties</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"cd3e154dc1b3bfce\" href=\"?note=cd3e154dc1b3bfce\" title=\"17-df-categoricity\">17-df-categoricity</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"0626faf5263e31f8\" href=\"?note=0626faf5263e31f8\" title=\"17-df-omega-stability\">17-df-omega-stability</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-thm-7.1.2"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> 为候选集合。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span> (sentences, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"1280f7fa724c1502\" href=\"?note=1280f7fa724c1502\" title=\"17-df-sentence\">17-df-sentence</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\)</span> (model class, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Consistent},\\operatorname{Complete}\">\\(\\operatorname{Consistent},\\operatorname{Complete}\\)</span> (consistency and completeness, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"bd7acd1192e46962\" href=\"?note=bd7acd1192e46962\" title=\"17-df-theory-properties\">17-df-theory-properties</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Categorical}_\\kappa\">\\(\\operatorname{Categorical}_\\kappa\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-categoricity, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"cd3e154dc1b3bfce\" href=\"?note=cd3e154dc1b3bfce\" title=\"17-df-categoricity\">17-df-categoricity</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Sym}(L)\">\\(\\operatorname{Sym}(L)\\)</span> (language symbol set, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"e8f9375543fc2e7d\" href=\"?note=e8f9375543fc2e7d\" title=\"17-df-language-cardinality\">17-df-language-cardinality</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S,|\\cdot|,\\aleph_0\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S,|\\cdot|,\\aleph_0\\)</span> (cardinality notions, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-13\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-14\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a>, and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-15\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\n&amp;T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Consistent}(T)\n\\land\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\n\\land\n\\aleph_0\\leq\\kappa\n\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n|\\operatorname{Sym}(L)|\\leq\\kappa\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Categorical}_\\kappa(T)\n\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n\\forall\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\aleph_0\\leq\\bigl|\\,|\\mathfrak M|\\,\\bigr|\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\operatorname{Complete}(T).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\n&amp;T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Consistent}(T)\n\\land\n\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\kappa)\n\\land\n\\aleph_0\\leq\\kappa\n\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n|\\operatorname{Sym}(L)|\\leq\\kappa\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Categorical}_\\kappa(T)\n\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n\\forall\\mathfrak M\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\aleph_0\\leq\\bigl|\\,|\\mathfrak M|\\,\\bigr|\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\operatorname{Complete}(T).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>If <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> were incomplete, the two incompatible completions would have models of size <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> by Löwenheim–Skolem, contradicting <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-categoricity. The no-finite-model condition and the language-size bound prevent vacuous uses of the test.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-language-cardinality","status":"resolved","id":"e8f9375543fc2e7d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-language-cardinality]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-sentence","status":"resolved","id":"1280f7fa724c1502","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-sentence]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-3","target